WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.332
The retail project asks you to build two different outputs from the same facts.

00:00:04.332 --> 00:00:07.082
The long table supports trend analysis.

00:00:07.082 --> 00:00:09.502
The wide table supports a scorecard.

00:00:09.502 --> 00:00:13.092
Both should represent the same revenue at different shapes.

00:00:13.092 --> 00:00:18.947
The project is not complete until you compare totals across the source and both reshaped outputs.

00:00:18.947 --> 00:00:24.992
Connect this idea to a machine-learning workflow converting wide measurements into tidy long data.

00:00:24.992 --> 00:00:31.612
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:31.612 --> 00:00:36.952
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:36.952 --> 00:00:42.812
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:42.812 --> 00:00:48.160
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
